# Excluded wholesale — it is a ~100 MB corpus of samples, audits and decision
# packages, none of which the runtime reads. The two exceptions below ARE runtime
# inputs: llm_config.txt (which ships in the image) points VOCAB_PATH at the
# vocabulary by default, and VocabularyManager reads taxonomy_config.json to decide
# which themes reach the model. Without them the published image was internally
# inconsistent — it shipped a config naming files it did not contain.
#
# That went unnoticed because a missing vocabulary used to fall back to a live AMCR
# harvest that silently produced a one-term category enum. The clients now refuse to
# auto-sync, so the image failed loudly instead (atrium-project run 34032532443),
# which is how this surfaced. `docker run <image> openrouter_client.py --input …`
# now works with no mounts and no --config, which is what the digital-born e2e and
# any ordinary user reasonably expect of a published tool image.
data_samples/
!data_samples/taxonomy_config.json
!data_samples/vocab/union_nested.json
TEMP/
*.log
*.png
*.html
.cache/
*.bin
*.pt
*.onnx
.env

# W8: the born-digital exploration corpus — 5.1 MB (sample.docx 3.0 MB,
# sample.pdf 1.98 MB, sample.pdf_docling_ir.json 197 KB) plus the Phase 0 probe
# scripts. These are research inputs for the pdfplumber-vs-PyMuPDF A/B, not
# runtime data, and they were being baked into EVERY published image (-remote and
# -llm today, -digital as of this change). The generated test fixtures under
# tests/fixtures/digital/ are 1-4 KB and are produced deterministically by
# make_fixtures.py, so nothing needs the big samples at runtime.
digital_born/
